From 7ae0c60065c7defb788f39d12a47008efa5745b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Willy Tarreau <w@1wt.eu>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:41:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] slz: add FIND_OPTIMAL_MATCH_MIN to try 3-byte matches

With FIND_OPTIMAL_MATCH, setting FIND_OPTIMAL_MATCH_MIN to 3 (default 4)
keys the hash chain on 3 bytes instead of 4, and takes a 3-byte match when
its code (7 bits of length plus the distance) is shorter than its three
literals (8 or 9 bits each). For ASCII text this means 3-byte matches up to
distance 8192. The text tree has no code for length 3, so they are dropped
there. SLZ_STATS's length histogram gets a bucket for 3.

